readme="# Original selected-Space prerequisite\n\nSource commit: "+source+". Parent: "+base+".\n\nThe original ActiveSpaceManager now retains exact account/request lifetimes, revokes before replacement/stop, serializes manager-owned transitions, drains admitted original WorkspaceOpen work and rejects stale callbacks. Opaque selection also retains the original callback-produced SpaceView generation when it existed at request creation; missing authority is not recaptured after suspension. The new statically dispatched Services extension accepts only the original final WorkspaceService and calls its unchanged original WorkspaceOpen method with the existing manager behavior withChat:true. Qualification's separate withChat:false path is not changed.\n\nThe ten new serialized Swift Testing groups passed once in the documented portable closure, along with complete original candidate parsing. The first wrapper failed afterward on a stdout-only emitted-binary-name assertion; that runner/traceback remain unchanged. The evidence-only continuation binds actual command receipts, fresh XML and matching named stdout, immutable original/compiled inputs and the emitted/linked PE, without inferring an independently observed OS child PID/invocation. The later evidence copy omission of XML/Package.swift/prior probe was corrected additively, preserving the complete earlier packet/index. Both continuations ran zero compilers/tests. Root independently reviewed the actual 91-file packet and all results.\n\nThe packet explicitly maps removed imports, test-only observation/counter additions and DI/publisher/subscription/native transport/value probes. It does not execute original native Invocation, Go, protobuf decoding, Apple frameworks or native UI. Shared widget/type/property readiness and native child shutdown, production auth/bootstrap, actual annotation destination factory/metadata/identity/body receipts/writer/ACK, device distribution and full StageB acceptance remain open. A retired admitted operation may have a side effect before its rejected return; no rollback is inferred.\n\nPublication initially stopped on three whitespace-only carried lines in the original activation/logging fragment. The exact canonical candidate already reviewed and tested retains that fragment with its eight-space dedent. The only three lint diagnostics are admitted through byte-bound original/candidate evidence; no whitespace rule is disabled and no source/test bytes change. Both the original lint stop and first read-only exact-indent proof failure are retained.\n\nSee evidence/CONTRACT_V2.md, evidence/CORRECTED_RESULT.json, evidence/TEST_RESULTS.xml, evidence/INDEX.json, independent-root-review/ROOT_REVIEW.json and SOURCE_PUBLICATION.json. No earlier test suite was replayed during this publication.\n"
write(doc/"README.md",readme)
